        "content": [
          "AI Parts Wizard finds duplicate parts bought under different part numbers across 4 plants and their models. Plants: HV0 (North Harvester Works), HV1 (South Harvester Works) build Harvesters; TR0 (East Tractor Works), TR1 (West Tractor Works) build Tractors. silver_parts: ~200K parts; part_id is the unique id; part_number is NOT globally unique so never join/group on it -- use part_id. Columns: part_category, material, description, dimensions, model_id, annual_volume (units purchased per year). silver_models: model_id -> plant_id + machine_type ('Harvester'/'Tractor'). silver_plants: plant_id -> name/location. gold_match_groups: near-duplicate clusters; group_id; savings_potential = ANNUAL savings in USD = sum over members of (member best unit price - group_best_price) x member annual_volume; total_current_spend = annual spend in USD; group_best_price = best unit price in USD; member_count; models_spanned/machine_types_spanned/plants_spanned (machine_types_spanned=2 spans harvesters AND tractors); avg_similarity (0-1). gold_match_group_members: group_id -> part_id with similarity (0-1). Join silver_parts for attrs, silver_models for machine_type/plant. silver_supplier_catalogs: per-supplier price_per_unit (USD), unit_discount, lead_time_days per part_id; join silver_suppliers for supplier_name. gold_normalized_parts/gold_review_dispositions: assigned enterprise part numbers and review status. similarity is 0-1 (95% similarity = similarity >= 0.95). Parts only match within the same part_category AND material. To answer 'harvester parts >95% similar to tractor part X': find X's group via gold_match_group_members, then its members joined to silver_models where machine_type='Harvester' and similarity >= 0.95. Example: total savings by category = SELECT part_category, round(sum(savings_potential),2) FROM gold_match_groups GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC. Cross-type groups = gold_match_groups WHERE machine_types_spanned > 1."
        ]
